# Godot 4+ specific ignores
.godot/
/android/

# Python bytecode. `tools/gen_prototype_assets.py` is importable (the art preview harness
# imports it), so CPython writes a __pycache__ next to it on every run.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Agent/CI scratch files (never commit). The `_` prefix is the agreed scratch convention
# (L-009): naming a helper `_probe.ps1` / `_out_x.log` makes it ignored by construction
# instead of relying on remembering to delete it.
_*.ps1
_*.log
*_tmp.txt
alive_probe.txt
commit_result.txt
push_result.txt
gitlog_tmp.txt

# LOCAL design-reference libraries (D-056 §40, D-057A) — reference-only, never assets.
#
# Classified, not ignored blindly (`docs/ASSET_LICENSES.md`, design-reference table):
#   * ui/source_packs/ — two CC0 1.0 upstream UI packs (34MB); exactly three files were ever
#     promoted, and those are tracked under `assets/ui/kenney_borders/`.
#   * aetheria_xianxia/ — the Aetheria art-direction moodboards: generated images with NO
#     recorded licence or rights, so research only (`docs/XIANXIA_IDENTITY_CONTRACT.md`).
# They stay OUT of git here, and OUT of `res://` through the tracked `docs/.gdignore` — being
# gitignored did not stop Godot importing the moodboards as game textures (D-057, L-044).
# Nothing in the project references this directory.
docs/design_refs/
